WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.560
The Arrowverse has become a complex web of&nbsp;
timelines, TV shows, and crossover events. Barry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.360
Allen, star of The Flash, is a wonderful entry&nbsp;
point into this shared universe, having started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:17.120
on Arrow and become a headlining hero in his own&nbsp;
right. This is his story, from beginning to end.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.120
By all accounts, Barry Allen had an ideal&nbsp;
childhood. His memories of it are filled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:28.640
with watching old musicals with his mother, Nora,&nbsp;
and traveling to museums with his father, Henry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:34.800
That would all change on March 18, 2000, when&nbsp;
Nora was killed by an inexplicable phenomenon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.120
Barry, startled by a commotion downstairs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.960
discovered his mother surrounded by strange&nbsp;
streaks of red and yellow lightning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.953
He briefly made out a man in yellow, tearing&nbsp;
through the room at impossible speeds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.600
When his father told him to run, Barry took off...&nbsp;
and suddenly found himself several blocks away.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.240
By the time Barry made it back to his home, his&nbsp;
father was being dragged away in handcuffs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.040
his mother was dead. Barry went to live with&nbsp;
the family of his closest friend, where his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.840
budding interest in science became a full-blown&nbsp;
obsession. Though he couldn't prove his father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:12.080
was innocent on his own, he knew there had to be&nbsp;
a way to exonerate him with concrete evidence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.480
He dedicated the rest of his schooling to&nbsp;
studying physics, chemistry, and criminology.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.880
Barry inhabits the Arrowverse, the CW's&nbsp;
live-action superhero canon. This shared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:29.280
universe began with Arrow, a 2012 series&nbsp;
centered around Oliver Queen, AKA Green Arrow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:34.400
Barry's beginning in the Arrowverse arrives in&nbsp;
the second season Arrow episode "The Scientist."

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.920
"Who the hell are you?"
"And do your parents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.160
know you're here?"
"I'm Barry Allen."

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.600
By this point in his life, Barry&nbsp;
Allen has become a criminologist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.280
still deeply troubled by his mother's&nbsp;
death. He travels to Star City&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.000
in the hopes of meeting his idol, Green&nbsp;
Arrow. He lies his way onto his team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.320
pretending to be working a case on behalf&nbsp;
of Central City's police department.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.560
While there, he impresses Green Arrow&nbsp;
by correctly figuring out a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:04.160
information about the way the masked vigilante&nbsp;
operates. Barry's story eventually falls apart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.000
however, forcing him to reveal that&nbsp;
he's looking to work on supernatural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.880
cases. If he can prove a case to be the work&nbsp;
of things beyond our current comprehension,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:17.760
he believes he'll be able to exonerate his&nbsp;
father and solve his mother's murder. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.400
solving a cold case and saving Green Arrow's&nbsp;
life, Allen hops a train back to Central City.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:28.800
After his adventures on Arrow, Barry Allen's&nbsp;
standalone story truly begins. On that train&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.760
back to Central City, he meets fellow physicist&nbsp;
Martin Stein, and the two quickly bond over their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:38.000
shared interest in a particle accelerator&nbsp;
project being run out of S.T.A.R. Labs.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.410
"They say it's gonna change the world."
"I hope so."

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.920
Even as Barry carries on his work&nbsp;
as a crime scene investigator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:49.215
he can't shake the idea of the work being&nbsp;
done by S.T.A.R.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:54.480
Barry's fixation is understandable - the particle&nbsp;
accelerator promises to reveal undiscovered realms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:59.600
of science. Since he has dedicated his life&nbsp;
to solving the mystery of his mother's death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:03.200
any grand expansion of scientific&nbsp;
understanding is of interest to Barry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.960
He didn't need to be enamored with the&nbsp;
accelerator for what came next, however:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.473
The massive machine explodes,&nbsp;
sending a shockwave across the city.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.668
Barry is struck by lightning through&nbsp;
a nearby window and falls into a coma.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.560
When he is hospitalized, the staff notice&nbsp;
all sorts of strange phenomena, including a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:26.480
constant flat-lining that has no ill effect upon&nbsp;
him. The mind behind S.T.A.R. Labs' accelerator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:31.040
Dr. Harrison Wells, realizes that Barry's&nbsp;
heart is beating too fast to register on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:34.800
hospital equipment. When it becomes clear&nbsp;
that they are dealing with something entirely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:38.800
out of the ordinary, a comatose Barry is&nbsp;
moved to S.T.A.R. for closer observation.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.640
Barry wakes after nine comatose months, and&nbsp;
quickly discovers that something is wrong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.520
with him. He heals from injuries rapidly,&nbsp;
and begins experiencing time dilation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:53.600
Moments slow down as his perception&nbsp;
heightens to impossible speed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:58.160
He runs, realizes that he's been given the&nbsp;
gift of super-speed, and sets about testing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:02.160
the limits of his new powers. In the course&nbsp;
of figuring out what's going on with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:06.960
Barry realizes that he's not alone in possessing&nbsp;
superpowers. In the wake of the accelerator's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.520
explosion, all sorts of Central City criminals&nbsp;
have developed extraordinary abilities.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:16.320
Barry comes to grips with his powers, and&nbsp;
begins to solve crimes and foil villains in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:21.120
Central City as the Flash. As he uncovers more&nbsp;
and more about the fallout of the explosion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.040
he begins to suspect that Dr.&nbsp;
Harrison Wells is not who he seems.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:32.922
"I don't know how, but he's the man in&nbsp;
yellow. Harrison Wells is the Reverse-Flash."

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.880
Everything comes to a head when&nbsp;
Barry's adoptive father Joe West&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:41.280
and his S.T.A.R. Labs' associate Cisco&nbsp;
Ramon uncover Harrison Wells' body.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:46.080
Barry's crew heads to the lab and discover&nbsp;
"Harrison Wells" to be a false persona.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.880
"This isn't possible."
"Caitlin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.880
I ran the DNA test twice. It's a perfect match."

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:56.720
They uncover a secret room containing&nbsp;
the yellow costume of the man Barry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:01.680
saw the night his mother died, as&nbsp;
well as a news clipping from 2024.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.640
The team works out that Wells&nbsp;
is someone from the future:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:11.200
Eobard Thawne, a villain known as Reverse-Flash,&nbsp;
who regularly battles the Flash in his own time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:16.240
He goes back to Barry's timeline to kill him as&nbsp;
a child, but is thwarted by a future version of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:21.440
the Flash, and ends up stuck in the past. He took&nbsp;
on Wells' identity to guide the lab toward making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:26.160
the particle accelerator. The explosion was an&nbsp;
intentional event to create the Flash, so that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:31.440
might harness Barry's abilities to return to his&nbsp;
own time. After several fights between Eobard and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:36.640
Barry, police detective Eddie Thawne realizes&nbsp;
that he can stop Eobard from ever existing.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.120
Since Eobard is a direct descendant of Eddie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:43.200
Eddie knows that killing himself would&nbsp;
cause Eobard to wink out of existence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:47.280
Eddie shoots himself with his service&nbsp;
pistol, and Eobard disappears.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:53.120
"I've controlled your life for so long,&nbsp;
Barry. How will you get along without me?"

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:58.640
The second season of The Flash gives Barry&nbsp;
a new nemesis. Like Eobard, he disguises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:04.560
himself as a friend, despite actually being from&nbsp;
another time and place. He is Hunter Zolomon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.960
and he has traveled to Barry's dimension through&nbsp;
a rift created by Eobard's disappearance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:14.720
Zolomon comes from another Earth, where he is a&nbsp;
serial killer obsessed with making himself fast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:17.920
He has traveled to Barry's Earth in&nbsp;
order to harvest his speed energy.

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:23.520
He disguises himself as Jay Garrick, a Flash&nbsp;
from yet another timeline, and befriends Barry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:28.320
All the while, he acts as the villainous Zoom,&nbsp;
giving Barry a reason to hone his powers - a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:34.640
process Jay helps with, naturally. Zolomon manages&nbsp;
to call forth a time remnant of himself so that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:40.160
Barry can see it die. Believing that his mentor&nbsp;
has been killed, Barry trains all the harder.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:44.880
Eventually, the S.T.A.R. Labs team learns of&nbsp;
Zolomon's true identity, leading to a showdown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:50.080
between Zoom and the Flash. He kills Flash's&nbsp;
father, Henry, and attempts to destroy the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:55.680
entire multiverse, but Barry outsmarts him using&nbsp;
the same time remnant trick Zoom used on him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:59.440
Time Wraiths pull Zoom out of the universe&nbsp;
and trap him within the Speed Force.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:05.200
Barry's entire life has been driven up to this&nbsp;
point by the dream of obtaining justice for his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:11.120
father. With his dad suddenly dead, Barry is&nbsp;
completely unmoored. He simply cannot tolerate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:16.240
any further suffering. He has lived his life in&nbsp;
pursuit of one goal - righting the wrong that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:20.400
has kept his living parent separated from&nbsp;
him - and that goal has been snatched away.

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:23.920
"I feel more broken than I've&nbsp;
ever felt in my entire life."

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:27.760
In spite of all he's learned about&nbsp;
timeline meddling being dangerous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:31.040
Barry runs back to the night his&nbsp;
mother died and saves her life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:37.440
He then beats Reverse-Flash unconscious and uses&nbsp;
a dampening cage to trap him in a prison in 2016.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:41.760
In this newly altered timeline, Barry begins&nbsp;
to lose the memories of his former life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:46.640
Surprisingly, Barry is still an investigator,&nbsp;
living a happy life with his family fully intact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:49.280
pursuing a relationship with&nbsp;
his childhood friend, Iris.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:55.600
Despite the seeming peace of this reality, all&nbsp;
is not well. Barry's treks around Central City&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:00.800
make him realize that his friends are suffering.&nbsp;
Iris' younger brother Wally West becomes the Flash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:05.600
in Barry's absence, but with nowhere near the&nbsp;
same level of support. Without the backing of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:10.160
a team like S.T.A.R. Labs, Wally runs himself&nbsp;
ragged fighting a villain called the Rival.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:15.040
Barry agrees to help Wally where he can,&nbsp;
but eventually sees that it is no use.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:19.280
After Wally is seriously hurt while fighting,&nbsp;
Barry is faced with a terrible choice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:24.000
He can reset the timeline by freeing Reverse-Flash&nbsp;
to kill his mother, or he can allow his friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:28.240
to continue suffering in the new world he has&nbsp;
wrought. Barry makes the choice you'd expect of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:34.000
a hero, taking Reverse-Flash back to the past. He&nbsp;
accepts that injustice to prevent a greater one.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:38.320
Once the timeline is restored, however, not&nbsp;
everything is back to where it once belonged.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:43.196
Relationships have changed, and fragments&nbsp;
from Flashpoint begin to find their way into&nbsp;&nbsp;Barry's world.

00:08:44.305 --> 00:08:49.340
Season three of The Flash had perhaps the&nbsp;
most-confusing villain in the history of the series.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:53.840
Savitar was a time remnant, a sort&nbsp;
of speedster super glue that works to stick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:58.880
together the space-time continuum whenever a Speed&nbsp;
Force user smashes it to bits with all their time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:04.160
travel. Savitar exists in a paradoxical&nbsp;
time loop. Essentially, by killing Iris,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:09.520
Savitar sets into motion the creation of the&nbsp;
time remnant that will eventually become Savitar.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.481
"And I only need two more things:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:19.760
for Iris to die, so that you can be driven&nbsp;
so far into the dark that I can be born."

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:24.400
In order to save his future wife, Barry and&nbsp;
his friends enlist the help of Earth-3's Flash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:27.280
Jay Garrick, to defeat Savitar once and for all.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:32.720
Barry and Iris finally take their marriage&nbsp;
vows during the fourth season of The Flash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:37.680
but the ceremony actually starts in a season&nbsp;
3 Supergirl episode. Friends of the bride and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:43.440
groom are at the proceedings when it's interrupted&nbsp;
by an assault from the villains of Earth-X — an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:48.960
alternate Earth where the Axis Powers won World&nbsp;
War II and subsequently conquered the globe. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:54.113
attack heralds the fourth of the Arrowverse's&nbsp;
annual crossover events, "Crisis on Earth-X."

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:58.880
The leaders of the "New Reichsmen" include&nbsp;
evil counterparts to the Arrowverse heroes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:05.280
like Dark Arrow Oliver Queen, and his wife&nbsp;
Overgirl, Earth-X's answer to Supergirl. Barry and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:11.040
many of the other Arrowverse heroes are captured&nbsp;
and placed in Earth-X's concentration camps.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:13.920
With the help of the Earth-X&nbsp;
heroes the Freedom Fighters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.800
Barry and the other heroes&nbsp;
are rescued. Tragically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:22.265
Martin Stein is mortally wounded while trying&nbsp;
to open a portal back to Earth-1 and later dies.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:25.200
After the heroes drive back the Earth-X assault,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:28.400
the wedding of Barry and Iris&nbsp;
is finally made official.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:34.960
The Flash's fourth season introduces a slew of&nbsp;
new baddies, all created by a single mastermind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:38.960
When Barry confronts this head honcho,&nbsp;
he finds a dying man in a wheelchair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:43.840
named Clifford DeVoe. He underestimates the&nbsp;
man, and Barry is framed for his murder.

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:49.440
DeVoe transfers his consciousness into the body of&nbsp;
one of the metahumans he created. While in prison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:54.560
Barry and a number of other metahumans nearly get&nbsp;
sold to a black market dealer in superpowers named&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.560 --> 00:11:00.080
Amunet Black. Barry is eventually able to clear&nbsp;
his name, and DeVoe continues to hop around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:05.440
bodies of those he created. The Flash and his&nbsp;
friends set about warning his remaining progeny.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:11.440
DeVoe reveals his plan: He hopes to use a series&nbsp;
of satellites to permanently rewire every human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:16.880
on Earth, a plot he calls "The Enlightenment."&nbsp;
Barry teams up with Amunet Black, and they destroy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:21.136
DeVoe's main satellite with a bomb procured&nbsp;
via their connection to illegal markets.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:26.560
DeVoe had planned for that eventuality, however.&nbsp;
He takes over the satellite system at S.T.A.R.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:32.400
Labs and initiates the Enlightenment. The Flash&nbsp;
very nearly fails to stop DeVoe, but a new Speed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:38.480
Force user named Nora appears and helps to stop&nbsp;
the destruction. But Nora comes bearing bad news:

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:44.468
"I think I made a big, big mistake."

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:50.000
Nora tells Barry and Iris that she is their&nbsp;
daughter from the future. She came back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:55.200
time to stop a new villain named Cicada, who&nbsp;
is an unstoppable force in her own timeline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:56.720
It is revealed throughout the season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.720 --> 00:12:00.720
as Barry and his allies attempt to mitigate&nbsp;
the havoc being wreaked on the timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:06.240
that Nora is regularly traveling back into the&nbsp;
future to work with the villainous Eobard Thawne.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:10.160
The bad guy, it seems, has earned Nora's&nbsp;
trust while imprisoned, and he's manipulated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:14.080
her into traveling to the past to set in&nbsp;
motion events that might set him free.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:19.360
A magical dagger that holds Thawne captive in a&nbsp;
prison of the future is destroyed in the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:24.480
allowing him to break out of prison and reappear&nbsp;
in the main timeline. The timeline-shifting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:28.320
ends in Nora winking out of existence,&nbsp;
leaving Barry and Iris without a daughter.

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:32.560
A lot of DC lore has come to the&nbsp;
screen over the last few decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:37.633
but until season 6 of The Flash, no one had&nbsp;
attempted to take on Crisis on Infinite Earths.

00:12:37.633 --> 00:12:41.040
As a villain known as the Anti-Monitor&nbsp;
threatened to wipe out all existence on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:46.080
the page, the landmark crossover comics&nbsp;
event gave DC a clean slate by wiping out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:51.200
the myriad parallel universes that had appeared&nbsp;
to account for decades of continuity problems.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:55.440
In creating a single, unified DC&nbsp;
universe, countless iterations of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:59.280
famous characters were killed. In the&nbsp;
comics, this included Barry Allen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:03.840
who sacrificed himself in a move that allowed&nbsp;
other heroes to defeat the Anti-Monitor.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:08.640
Television's Arrowverse saw a similarly&nbsp;
cataclysmic restart in season 6 of The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:13.440
Flash — and viewers who only knew Barry&nbsp;
through Grant Gustin's portrayal finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:16.640
came to understand the terms&nbsp;
"pre-Crisis" and "post-Crisis."

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:20.400
Season 6 of The Flash begins&nbsp;
with Barry learning that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.200
Crisis is coming sooner than Team Flash had hoped.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:32.800
"December 10, 2019. On that day he will answer&nbsp;
the call. And make the ultimate sacrifice."

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:36.400
It becomes clear that the Flash will die&nbsp;
during the multiverse-wide shakeup, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:41.120
Barry begins preparing all of his friends, family&nbsp;
and fellow crimefighters for a world without him.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:45.600
At the same time, a villain called Bloodwork&nbsp;
threatens Central City. Bloodwork is attempting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:50.240
to find a cure for a deadly disease that runs in&nbsp;
his family, but the treatment he found turned him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:55.151
monstrous and filled him with a need for the blood&nbsp;
of others to maintain an eternal life. At some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.151 --> 00:13:59.600
point, he realizes that his blood can effectively&nbsp;
control others if it gets into their system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:04.400
and he sets out to create an army of "Blood&nbsp;
Brothers." Bloodwork's quest for never-ending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:09.120
life and Barry accepting his fate are played&nbsp;
as mirrors of each other throughout the season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:13.360
even as Allen is infected and controlled&nbsp;
by the villain. Bloodwork's master plan to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:18.640
infect the entire city ultimately backfires,&nbsp;
and all of his minions are returned to normal.

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:22.720
In their confrontation with the Anti-Monitor,&nbsp;
another Flash named Barry Allen from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:27.040
different part of the multiverse ends up&nbsp;
sacrificing himself to save existence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:31.360
Barry Allen does die, it turns out —&nbsp;
just not the one who leads The Flash.

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:33.901
"Sorry kid. But this has to happen."

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:40.720
The season closes with Barry attempting to carry&nbsp;
on in a newly created multiverse that only he and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:46.480
a few other metahumans know is not the world as&nbsp;
it was. His actions during the Crisis also destroy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:51.280
the Speed Force, the borderline mystical reserve&nbsp;
of energy from which speedsters pull their powers.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:57.520
After the events of Crisis on Infinite Earths,&nbsp;
Barry and Wally learn the Speed Force is in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:02.320
trouble. Confronting the Speed Force's human&nbsp;
manifestation, Barry learns that when Oliver Queen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:08.560
used his Spectre powers to get Barry back into the&nbsp;
Speed Force during Crisis, it contaminated things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:15.040
The Speed Force seemingly dies, leaving Barry and&nbsp;
Wally only weeks of residual speedster powers.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:19.920
With the help of Nora West-Allen's diary,&nbsp;
Team Flash builds an Artificial Speed Force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:25.680
that Barry can access, but once again the cost&nbsp;
is too high. Even though Nash Wells sacrifices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:31.280
himself to power the ASF with his multiversal&nbsp;
energy, Team Flash learns the ASF is causing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:36.240
Barry's thinking to go as fast as his body, with&nbsp;
catastrophic consequences to his personality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:41.280
Once Barry realizes what's happening to him,&nbsp;
he disables the new source of his powers.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:43.840
But with the help of the&nbsp;
re-emerged Harrison Wells,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:46.800
the residual Speed Force within Iris and the ASF,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:51.840
Team Flash later succeeds in essentially rebooting&nbsp;
the Speed Force, giving Barry back his powers.

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:57.280
On the night of the S.T.A.R. Labs particle&nbsp;
accelerator explosion, Eva McCulloch is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:02.560
killed as she's thrown into a mirror. The dark&nbsp;
matter creates a mirror-universe duplicate of Eva&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:08.320
with all of her memories stuck in the Mirrorverse&nbsp;
- a universe governed by different physical laws.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:13.520
The new Mirror Eva tricks Iris into allowing&nbsp;
herself to be pulled into the Mirrorverse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:16.960
while a mirror duplicate of Iris&nbsp;
replaces her on Earth-Prime.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:21.680
After also capturing and creating duplicates&nbsp;
of Singh and Cisco's girlfriend Kamilla,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:26.320
Eva, now calling herself MIrror&nbsp;
Monarch, finally escapes to Earth-Prime.

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:31.120
Mirror Monarch plans to take over the globe by&nbsp;
replacing everyone with mirror counterparts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:34.400
and Barry is distracted, dealing&nbsp;
with the death of the Speed Force.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:39.840
Once it's restored, Barry and Iris are able to&nbsp;
stop Mirror Monarch's plans and make her see the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:44.960
error of her ways. She returns Earth-Prime's&nbsp;
people and retreats to the Mirrorverse.

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:50.160
But it's clear that Mirror Monarch has left a&nbsp;
dark scar on Central City. Iris joins a support&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:54.960
group founded specifically to help those who&nbsp;
were abducted and traumatized by the villain.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:57.200
Check out one of our newest&nbsp;
videos right here! Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:00.560
even more Looper videos about your&nbsp;
favorite Arrowverse heroes are coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:04.226
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit&nbsp;
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

